---
// What Sub20 is for, one game clip from plan to Discord in three steps: the plan row's size and verdict
// (plan.webp), the finished file, 248 MB down to 19.4 MB (done.webp), then the clip arriving in a chat.
// The same story on both paths, written once: the desktop app's in #download (`path="app"`, hidden where
// the desktop app doesn't run) and Lite's in #lite (`path="lite"`, shown only there). Only the third
// step's words differ: the desktop copies with Ctrl+C; Lite shares on a touch screen and downloads with a
// mouse, by the app's own rule (`pointer: coarse`). Every picture is a picture, never a control: crops of
// the screenshots (site.css), and the chat drawn in the site's own palette and fonts, not any chat app's.
// Both copies ask for the same files (one name and `sizes` each), so the hidden one costs nothing, and
// they carry no ids. The sizes are said in words at body size, since the crops draw them small.
import Shot from "./Shot.astro";

interface Props {
  /** "app": the desktop app's hand-off (Copy). "lite": Sub20 Lite's (Share on a touch screen, else Download). */
  path: "app" | "lite";
  class?: string;
}
const { path, class: classes } = Astro.props;
---

<div class:list={["frame payoff", classes]}>
  <ol class="payoff__story" role="list">
    <li>
      <p>Before it starts, Sub20 says how it will look</p>
      <div class="payoff__crop payoff__crop--plan">
        <Shot name="plan" alt="Sub20's plan for a 41 s game clip: 1440p, H.264 at 3.9 Mbps, Should look good" sizes="800px" />
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>When it's done, the clip is <strong>19.4&nbsp;MB</strong>, down from 248&nbsp;MB</p>
      <div class="payoff__crop payoff__crop--done">
        <Shot name="done" alt="The finished file: clutch-1v4-ranked-20mb.mp4, 19.4 MB, down from 248 MB" sizes="720px" />
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      {path === "app" ? (
        <p>Copy it with Ctrl+C, then paste it in Discord</p>
      ) : (
        <p><span class="payoff__touch">Tap Share, then pick Discord</span><span class="payoff__mouse">Download it, then drop it in Discord</span></p>
      )}
      <div class="payoff__chat" role="img" aria-label="A chat message from You with the clip attached: clutch-1v4-ranked-20mb.mp4, 19.4 MB">
        <span class="payoff__avatar">Y</span>
        <div class="payoff__message">
          <span class="payoff__who">You</span>
          <div class="payoff__file">
            <div class="payoff__crop payoff__crop--thumb"><Shot name="done" alt="" sizes="720px" /></div>
            <span class="payoff__name">clutch-1v4-ranked-20mb.mp4</span>
            <span class="payoff__size">19.4&nbsp;MB</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ol>
</div>
